# Running the browser client against the COMPOSE stack.
#
# ⚠️ Nothing goes in this file for the usual case. The client talks to its OWN origin
# and the Vite dev server proxies onward, so the stack's ports live in vite.config.ts
# and nowhere else. Point the dev server at compose's published ports instead:
#
#   ZB_BRIDGE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:9090 ZB_NATS_WS_ORIGIN=ws://127.0.0.1:8080 npm run dev
#
# (substitute whatever BRIDGE_PUBLISH_PORT and NATS_WS_PUBLISH_PORT are set to — with
# the native stack also running they have to be moved, e.g. 9098 and 8081.)
#
# The compose broker is the PRE-OPERATOR world: `authorization { users: … }` with
# password principals and the bridge's nkey — no operator, no resolver. So the
# /enroll flow does NOT apply there (a minted JWT has nothing to validate it, and the
# bridge answers `enrollment not configured` because ZB_SIGNING_SEED and
# ZB_ACCOUNT_PUB are deliberately absent from .env.docker). Connect as a declared
# principal; scripts/native/ is the stack that mints creds.
VITE_PRINCIPAL=alice
VITE_PASSWORD=s3cret

# Only for a page NOT served by the Vite dev server — a built bundle behind the
# compose `edge` nginx, which fronts both on one port:
#   VITE_NATS_URL=ws://localhost:8090/nats
#   VITE_BRIDGE_URL=http://localhost:8090
